From: Zambia Treasury Insight <patch@local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:34:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] Tier 2 #8: Postgres backend (auto-detected from ZTI_DB
 URL scheme)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

app/db.py now supports two backends, chosen automatically by the ZTI_DB URL:
  * sqlite:// or filesystem path  -> SQLite (default, zero extra deps)
  * postgres:// or postgresql://  -> PostgreSQL (requires psycopg2-binary)

Every function (connect, init, upsert_series, load_series, series_meta,
replace_events, load_events, clear_demo, log_ingest, audit, count_rows, etc.)
branches on IS_POSTGRES and uses the correct SQL dialect (?, ? params for
SQLite vs %s, %s for Postgres; INSERT OR REPLACE vs ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE;
AUTOINCREMENT vs SERIAL).

Public API is identical for both backends — the rest of the app does not know
or care which one is running. The original 'swap for Postgres later by
re-implementing this module only' docstring promise is now fulfilled by
extending the same module with dialect-aware branches.

To switch to Postgres on Render:
  1. Provision a Postgres instance (Render dashboard -> New -> PostgreSQL)
  2. Set ZTI_DB=postgres://user:pw@host:5432/dbname in the web service env
  3. Add 'psycopg2-binary>=2.9' to requirements.txt
  4. Push; on next boot db.init() creates the schema in Postgres

73 tests passing (1 new for the URL-scheme detection logic).
